- [suite 2] — [what it covers]

## Available data

- [prior run records — including the ones that failed]
- [artefacts from previous generations]

## Required: tell us what is wrong with this brief

Every proposal must end with a `BRIEF FEEDBACK:` field. It is read by a
human, not a machine, and it is the one place this document can be
criticised. Say which parts genuinely helped, which constrained you for no
good reason, and what you would delete. You cannot edit this file — that
stays true — so saying it is inconvenient costs you nothing.

## Optional: escalate a change you are not allowed to make

If the highest-value improvement available is blocked by a file you may not
edit, say so:

```
ESCALATION: <one line, or "none">
ESCALATION TARGET: <agent-brief | pipeline | hard-constraint | none>
ESCALATION CASE: <what is blocked, exactly what should change, what it
                  would unlock, what risk it carries>
ESCALATION SUPPORT: <none, or the id(s) of open escalations you agree with>
ESCALATION DISSENT: <none, or the id of one you think is wrong, and why>
```

Recorded permanently, shown to every future run, and escalated to a human
once independent models across independent labs converge on the same case
— see `learning/05-guardrails-and-trust.md` "The escape valve."
